{"name":"Hematite","hex":"#5f615f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hematite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An iron ore, mainly peroxide of iron, Fe2O3: iron(III) oxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hematite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hematite","blocks":[{"text":"Hematite ( HE(E)M-ə-tyte), also spelled as haematite, is a common iron oxide compound with the formula Fe2O3 and is widely found in rocks and soils. Hematite crystals belong to the rhombohedral lattice system which is designated the alpha polymorph of Fe2O3. It has the same crystal structure as corundum (Al2O3) and ilmenite (FeTiO3). With this crystal structure geometry it forms a complete solid solution at temperatures above 950 °C (1,740 °F)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/WLA_hmns_Hematite.jpg/330px-WLA_hmns_Hematite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hematite","wikidata":"Q103223"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Hematite_structure.jpg/500px-Hematite_structure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Hematite_structure.jpg/500px-Hematite_structure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crystal structure of hematite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHematite_structure.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/07-ml-3-soil-mosaic-B019R1_br.jpg/500px-07-ml-3-soil-mosaic-B019R1_br.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/07-ml-3-soil-mosaic-B019R1_br.jpg/1280px-07-ml-3-soil-mosaic-B019R1_br.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo